  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#33774\", \"PowerToys#4987\", \"PowerToys#10497\"], \"answer\": \"This feature request has been made before. Keyboard Manager (KBM) can't currently apply mappings only for a particular input method or keyboard layout. PowerToys#33774 asks for KBM profiles tied to IMEs, and the maintainers agreed it is a needed feature. They said that if the IME switch can be detected, switching profiles automatically would be possible. PowerToys#4987 asks for a remap that applies only to one language layout. PowerToys#10497 asks for remapping that depends on the input mode. None of these has been implemented, and I found no official fix. Add a 👍 to #33774 and describe your scenario there. The related request for general KBM profiles is PowerToys#1881. Until then, you can switch mappings by hand. Keep separate KBM config JSON files in %LocalAppData%\\\\Microsoft\\\\PowerToys\\\\Keyboard Manager. Copy the one you want over default.json and restart PowerToys.KeyboardManagerEngine.exe, as described in #1881. A script can do this. AutoHotkey can also apply remaps per layout.\"}",
